1. Introduction

Objective

The objective of this project is to evaluate and improve the performance of machine learning regression models using model validation techniques. The project focuses on detecting overfitting, applying cross-validation, performing hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV, and selecting the best-performing model based on evaluation metrics.

Dataset

The California Housing Dataset from scikit-learn was used for this project. The dataset contains housing-related features such as median income, house age, average rooms, average bedrooms, population, occupancy, latitude, and longitude. The target variable is the median house value.

2. Data Preparation

The dataset was divided into features (X) and target variable (y). Feature scaling was performed using StandardScaler to standardize the numerical features. The dataset was then split into training and testing sets using an 80:20 ratio.

3. Overfitting Analysis

A Decision Tree Regressor was initially trained using default parameters.
To identify overfitting, the model performance on both training and testing datasets was compared.
Overfitting occurs when a model learns the training data too closely and fails to generalize well to unseen data.
The training RMSE and testing RMSE were calculated. A significant difference between these values indicated that the model was overfitting the training data.
Observation
Training RMSE: ______
Testing RMSE: ______
The lower training error and higher testing error suggested that the baseline Decision Tree model had overfitting issues.

4. Cross-Validation

To obtain a more reliable estimate of model performance, 5-fold cross-validation was applied.
Cross-validation divides the dataset into five subsets. During each iteration, four subsets are used for training and one subset is used for validation. The process repeats five times and the average score is calculated.
Result:
Cross-validation RMSE: ______
The cross-validation score provided a better estimate of how the model would perform on unseen data.

5. Hyperparameter Tuning

GridSearchCV was used to improve the Decision Tree model by finding the best hyperparameter combination.
The following parameters were tuned:
max_depth
min_samples_split
GridSearchCV evaluated all parameter combinations using 5-fold cross-validation and selected the best-performing model.
Best Parameters
max_depth: ______
min_samples_split: ______

6. Model Evaluation

Three models were evaluated:
Linear Regression
Ridge Regression
Tuned Decision Tree
The evaluation metrics used were:
RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)
RMSE measures the average prediction error. Lower RMSE values indicate better performance.
R² Score
R² measures how well the model explains the variation in the target variable. Higher R² values indicate better performance.
