8. Final Model Justification

Based on the evaluation results, the Tuned Decision Tree model was selected as the final model.
Reasons:
Achieved the best balance between bias and variance.
Produced a lower RMSE compared to the baseline model.
Achieved a higher R² score.
Hyperparameter tuning reduced overfitting and improved generalization performance.
Cross-validation confirmed stable performance across multiple folds.

9. Conclusion

This project demonstrated the importance of model validation and hyperparameter tuning in machine learning.Cross-validation was used to estimate model performance more reliably, while GridSearchCV helped identify the optimal Decision Tree configuration. The tuned model achieved improved performance compared to the baseline models and was selected as the final solution.